From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meridian <meridian@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:55:36 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 115/297] Meridian: builds and runs on Linux; the Windows side
 of the same seams

What only macOS had, behind the same interfaces:
- Workbench "Move to Trash": gio trash on Linux, the Recycle Bin on Windows.
- AskNative (the Workbench's and the agent's questions): a browser-modal
  views dialog, a button per answer, the first one the default.
- Mission Control's platform part: the last active browser window stands in
  for NSApp; no Dock badge.
- Default browser (welcome tour, Settings): Chromium's DefaultBrowserWorker.
- chrome://workbench finds its files next to the executable, as the ad
  blocking rules already do.
- The updater replaces a signed Meridian.app with macOS's tools, so it is
  built on macOS only; elsewhere a stub reports this build's version.
Also two includes macOS got by way of other headers, a full traffic
annotation for the agent's local socket (the short form doesn't exist on
Windows and Linux), libutil for openpty, and chdir's result in the terminal.
